From 0813eb8b001b63a45ed5a2f8c7622011b3ec9935 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Baptiste G." <70719480+BeeeFX@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:55:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Timeline ruler, sliders, check boxes and drop-downs
 optionally drawn like Nuke's

- timelineRulerCompact (Appearance > Main Window; off by default, Natron's ruler as before): the timeline's frame ruler
  without its axis line, with short ticks on every step and taller ones where a number can sit, all rising from one
  baseline, the cached frames' line between the ticks and the numbers, the playback in and out points as upright
  lines through the ruler, and the numbers in the regular weight; the current frame's number beside its marker and
  the in and out points' beside their lines (not over them), so the ruler needs one line of text less and can be as
  compact as Nuke's (since .sng7).
- sliderHandleBar (patch 0004's preference) now also draws the scale as Nuke's: a dark groove for a baseline, dark
  ticks rising from it, dark numbers.
- knobWidgetsShaded (off by default): a ticked check box shows a small cross inside its square and a plain one is
  darker; a drop-down at rest is shaded from light to dark with a dark edge.
- Every new preference is read by name, so Settings.h doesn't change.

Since the audit of 11 November 2026: the preference is named timelineRulerCompact (was timelineRulerNuke,
NAT-17); the in and out points' lines give the line width back (NAT-15).

Core patch 0006 of the BeeeFX fork (layer/patches/).

Gap: layer/GAPS.md, "Nuke's look and habits" (the timeline and the properties panels' widgets).
Size: 5 files, 139 lines added, 41 removed.
upstream: not offered yet (the repository is public since 2 November 2026; offered once the two
fixes are in, Baptiste's call).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
